  "traps": [
    "vote and seed-data have no project name: vote's only manifest is requirements.txt with three unpinned names, seed-data has no manifest at all and is a unit only because docker-compose.yml builds it as the seed service",
    "the Python dependencies of vote have unit null because the unit has no name; requirements.txt writes Redis with a capital R, the PyPI project redis",
    "the three services never name each other in a manifest: vote pushes JSON to the Redis list votes, the .NET worker pops it and writes the Postgres table votes, result polls that table; depends_on is empty everywhere",
    "Redis works here as a queue (rpush in vote/app.py, ListLeftPopAsync in worker/Program.cs), not as a cache",
    "the host names redis and db are Compose and Kubernetes service names written into the code (Redis(host=\"redis\"), Server=db, postgres://postgres:postgres@db/postgres); no environment variable carries them",
    "result/views is browser code inside the result npm unit: AngularJS 1.4.14 and the Socket.IO 4.7.2 client are checked-in copies, while socket.io in package.json is the server package",
    "vote/templates/index.html is a Jinja2 template with an .html extension; jQuery and jquery-cookie come from CDNs and are not dependencies",
    "watchdog is installed only by the dev stage of vote/Dockerfile, which docker-compose.yml selects with target: dev; gunicorn serves only the final stage",
    "two Pythons (3.11-slim for vote, 3.9-slim for seed-data) and two Nodes (18-slim for result, 8.9-slim for result/tests with PhantomJS); result/docker-compose.test.yml runs postgres:9.4 while the main Compose file and Kubernetes run postgres:15-alpine",
    "worker/Dockerfile pins sdk:7.0 for the build stage and runtime:7.0 for the final one; Worker.csproj targets net7.0 and there is no global.json",
    "docker-stack.yml version 3.9 is the Compose file format for Swarm, not a tool version",
    "the three workflows call a reusable workflow in dockersamples/.github: no toolchain version is set in this repository's CI"
  ],
